    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Human activities often place great pressure on the environment, resulting in <span class="learn-keyword">environmental problems</span> such as pollution, deforestation, desertification, soil erosion, and overpopulation.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Pollution</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Cause</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Air pollution</td><td>Vehicle exhaust, industrial emissions, gas flaring</td><td>Respiratory diseases, acid rain, climate change</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Water pollution</td><td>Dumping of waste, oil spillage, sewage discharge</td><td>Contaminated drinking water, death of aquatic life</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Land pollution</td><td>Improper waste disposal, use of chemicals/pesticides</td><td>Soil contamination, reduced fertility</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Noise pollution</td><td>Loud machinery, traffic, generators</td><td>Hearing damage, stress, reduced concentration</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Deforestation</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Deforestation</span> is the large-scale clearing of forests, mainly for farming, logging, and urban expansion. It leads to loss of biodiversity, soil erosion, reduced rainfall, and increased carbon dioxide levels.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Desertification</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Desertification</span> is the process by which fertile land becomes desert, typically due to drought, deforestation, overgrazing, and poor farming practices. Northern Nigeria is particularly affected by desertification.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Soil Erosion</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Soil erosion</span> is the wearing away and removal of the top fertile layer of soil by water or wind, often worsened by deforestation, overgrazing, and poor farming methods. Gully erosion is a severe form common in South-Eastern Nigeria.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Overpopulation</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Overpopulation</span> occurs when the number of people in an area exceeds the resources and infrastructure available to sustain them comfortably, leading to overcrowding, resource scarcity, and increased pollution and waste.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to link causes to effects for each environmental problem (e.g., "how does deforestation contribute to soil erosion and desertification?"). Also study Nigerian examples like gully erosion in the South-East and desertification in the North.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Major environmental problems include pollution (air, water, land, noise), deforestation, desertification, soil erosion, and overpopulation — all largely driven by human activities and requiring urgent management.\n</div>\n  ',
