    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Environmental conservation</span> refers to the deliberate protection, preservation, and wise management of natural resources and the environment to prevent depletion and degradation.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Environmental Conservation</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Environmental conservation is the careful and planned management of natural resources and ecosystems to protect them from destruction, depletion, or degradation, ensuring they remain available and healthy for both present and future use.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Methods of Environmental Conservation</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Afforestation</td><td>Planting trees on land that previously had no forest</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reforestation</td><td>Replanting trees in areas where forests have been cleared</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Legislation</td><td>Government laws and policies that regulate resource use and protect the environment (e.g., anti-pollution laws)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Recycling</td><td>Reprocessing waste materials (plastic, metal, paper) into new products, reducing raw material extraction</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Controlled grazing</td><td>Regulating livestock movement and grazing areas to prevent overgrazing and land degradation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Additional Conservation Practices</h3>\n<ul class="learn-list">\n  <li>Creation of protected areas such as national parks and game reserves</li>\n  <li>Terracing and contour ploughing to reduce soil erosion on slopes</li>\n  <li>Proper waste management and treatment before disposal</li>\n  <li>Public education and awareness campaigns on environmental protection</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Importance of Conservation</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Conservation ensures the continued availability of resources, protects biodiversity, maintains ecological balance, reduces the risk of natural disasters (like flooding from deforested land), and supports sustainable economic development.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish clearly between afforestation (planting where there was no forest before) and reforestation (replanting where forest was cleared) — this distinction is a common exam trap.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Environmental conservation protects natural resources through methods like afforestation, reforestation, legislation, recycling, and controlled grazing, ensuring resources remain available and ecosystems stay healthy for future generations.\n</div>\n  ',
