    module: 'Economic Geography',
    term: 'Second Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Commercial activities</span> involve the buying, selling, and exchange of goods and services. In Nigeria, trade, banking, insurance, and tourism together form a vital part of the economy.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning and Types of Commercial Activities</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Trade</td><td>Buying and selling of goods and services, either internally (domestic trade) or internationally (import/export)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Banking</td><td>Provision of financial services such as savings, loans, and money transfer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Protection against financial loss from risks such as accidents, fire, or theft, in exchange for premium payments</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Tourism</td><td>Travel to and visiting of places for leisure, culture, or business purposes</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Role of Trade in Nigeria\'s Economy</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Trade links producers to consumers, both locally and internationally. Nigeria trades commodities like crude oil, cocoa, and solid minerals internationally while engaging in extensive domestic trade of food crops and manufactured goods within its local markets.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Role of Banking and Insurance</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Banks mobilize savings and provide credit that fuels business investment, agriculture, and industry. Insurance companies help individuals and businesses manage financial risk, encouraging investment by reducing the fear of catastrophic loss.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Role of Tourism</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Tourism generates foreign exchange, creates jobs in hospitality and related services, and promotes cultural exchange. Nigeria has tourism potential through sites like the Obudu Cattle Ranch, Yankari Game Reserve, Olumo Rock, and various cultural festivals.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Contribution to Nigeria\'s Economy</h3>\n<ul class="learn-list">\n  <li>Generates employment across trading, financial, and hospitality sectors</li>\n  <li>Contributes to government revenue through taxes and levies</li>\n  <li>Facilitates the flow of goods, capital and people, supporting overall economic growth</li>\n  <li>Attracts foreign investment and tourists, boosting foreign exchange earnings</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> WAEC often asks how banking or insurance supports economic development — always link your answer to how they enable investment by mobilizing capital or reducing financial risk.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Commercial activities — trade, banking, insurance and tourism — connect producers, consumers, and investors, generating employment, government revenue, and foreign exchange, and playing a vital role in Nigeria\'s overall economic development.\n</div>\n  ',
