    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Settlements do not exist in isolation — rural and urban areas constantly interact through the movement of people, goods, and services, most notably through <span class="learn-keyword">rural-urban migration</span>.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Settlement Interaction</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Settlement interaction</span> refers to the flow of people, goods, services, and information between different settlements, especially between rural and urban areas.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Rural-Urban Migration</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Rural-urban migration</span> is the movement of people from rural (countryside) areas to urban (city) areas, usually in search of better opportunities.</p>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Push Factors (from rural areas)</th><th>Pull Factors (to urban areas)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Limited job opportunities</td><td>More varied and better-paying jobs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Poor infrastructure and social amenities</td><td>Better schools, hospitals, and infrastructure</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Low agricultural income</td><td>Prospects of higher income</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Land fragmentation/scarcity</td><td>Access to modern lifestyle and entertainment</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Effects of Rural-Urban Interaction</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Rural areas</td><td>Loss of youthful labor force, reduced agricultural productivity, but may benefit from remittances sent by migrants</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Urban areas</td><td>Overpopulation, pressure on housing and infrastructure, unemployment, growth of slums, increased crime</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Problems Arising from Settlement Interactions</h3>\n<ul class="learn-list">\n  <li>Rural depopulation and aging farming population</li>\n  <li>Urban overcrowding and slum development</li>\n  <li>Strain on urban housing, water, and sanitation services</li>\n  <li>Rising urban unemployment as migrants outnumber available jobs</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Solutions</h3>\n<ul class="learn-list">\n  <li>Rural development programs to improve infrastructure and income opportunities</li>\n  <li>Decentralization of industries and services away from a few large cities</li>\n  <li>Investment in agriculture to make rural livelihoods more attractive</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Learn push and pull factors as a matched pair, and be ready to discuss effects on BOTH rural and urban areas — WAEC often requires balanced coverage of both sides.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Settlement interaction, especially rural-urban migration, is driven by push factors (from rural areas) and pull factors (to urban areas). It affects rural areas through labor loss and urban areas through overcrowding, requiring rural development and decentralization as solutions.\n</div>\n  ',
